BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.levyparkhousto
 n.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/I63A4918-scaled.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.levyparkhouston.org/wp-content/upload
 s/2026/05/I63A4918-scaled.jpg
UID:LlOEsY23i0IL2FGO4dEwZ
SUMMARY:Free Watch Party: Norway vs England (4pm) and Switzerland/Colombia 
	vs Argentina (8pm)
DTSTAMP:20260708T050911Z
DTSTART:20260711T143000Z
DESCRIPTION:Three days of quarterfinal madness wrap up tonight\, and the st
	akes couldn’t be higher. By the final whistle\, we’ll know our four semifi
	nalists. Don’t miss the moment it all becomes clear. \nKickoff for Norway 
	vs England is at 4:00 p.m. Kickoff for Game 2 is at 8:00 p.m. Admission is
	 free! \nCommunity Partners: Supporting this event is the Houston Show Cho
	ir. Houston Show Choir is made up of talented adult singers who perform an
	 entertaining\, diverse repertoire with lively choreography. They produce 
	two big shows every year in June and December and perform at community eve
	nts throughout the year. Their vision is “to share the joy of music”\, if 
	that resonates with you\, auditions are in August and January! Email direc
	tor@houstonshowchoir or follow us on Facebook/Instagram for more info! \nF
	ace Painting & Henna Art: Get into the tournament spirit with face and bod
	y art from Gio’s Art Kreations and Henna Station & Glitter Bar \nMerchandi
	se: Event merchandise celebrating Houston\, Levy Park\, and the global soc
	cer tournament will also be available for purchase. \nArt Installations an
	d Photo Opportunities: Commemorate the experience with a photo tour of the
	 park\, including life-sized soccer-themed photo backdrops and a tournamen
	t bracket. Visit our soccer ball music box and turn the crank for festive 
	sounds. \nFestival Guidelines: \nVISITORS MUST COMPLY WITH DIRECTIONS FROM
	 PARK PERSONNEL\, OR THEY WILL BE ASKED TO LEAVE THE PARK. PARENTS ARE RES
	PONSIBLE FOR THEIR CHILDREN’S SAFETY IN THE PARK. \nCHAIRS AND SEATING: No
	 outside furniture. Blankets may be brought into the Festival site for the
	 designated blanket seating area. All other furniture is available on a fi
	rst-come\, first-served basis. \nSTROLLERS & WAGONS: Oversized strollers a
	nd wagons may need to be parked in a designated area during the festival. 
	All visitors must comply with park personnel regarding stroller and wagon 
	parking. \nFOOD AND BEVERAGES: Guests are permitted to enter with one fact
	ory-sealed bottle of water. To go food from Kind Ice Cream\, Hearsay\, and
	 Gaspachos is also welcome inside the festival site along with one factory
	 sealed drink per person. Other outside food and drinks are prohibited (ex
	ceptions will be made for baby food and necessary medical dietary food ite
	ms). A variety of food\, non-alcoholic drinks\, beer\, and wine will be av
	ailable for purchase from Festival concessionaires. \nRE-ENTRY: If you lea
	ve the Festival site\, you will be re-screened before re-entry. \nTHE FOLL
	OWING ARE PROHIBITED: \n\nSmoking or Vaping\nUmbrellas\nDrug Use\nKites an
	d Drones\nRecreational Motorized Vehicles\nGuns\, knives\, any weaponry\nS
	oliciting\nBikes\, scooters\, rollerblades\, and roller skates\n\nhttps://
	www.levyparkhouston.org/events/quarterfinals-double-header/\n\nFrom Levy P
	ark Houston
URL:https://www.levyparkhouston.org/events/quarterfinals-double-header/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:levy-park-houston
CATEGORIES:Levy Park Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT9H
END:VEVENT
